{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"kind\":\"final\",\"decision\":\"answer\",\"answer\":754,\"evidence\":[\"receipt-1\"],\"confidence\":0.99,\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"reason\":\"Dynamic programming counting binary strings of length 13 avoiding 000 and 111\"}","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 13 that avoid forbidden substrings \"000\" and \"111\". So no three consecutive same bits. Count sequences of length n with no run of 3 same bits. Classic recurrence: Let a_n be number of sequences length n ending with run of length 1 of some bit, b_n ending with run of length 2. For n=1: a1=2 (0 or1), b1=0. For n>1: new a_n = a_{n-1}+b_{n-1} (since can append opposite bit to any previous run). new b_n = a_{n-1} (since to have run length 2, previous must have run length1 and same bit appended). So recurrence: a_n = a_{n-1}+b_{n-1}; b_n = a_{n-1}. Also total t_n = a_n + b_n. We can compute quickly up to 13.\n\nLet's compute:\n\nn=1: a1=2, b1=0, t1=2\nn=2: a2 = a1+b1=2+0=2; b2 = a1=2; t2=4\nn=3: a3 = a2+b2=2+2=4; b3 = a2=2; t3=6\nn=4: a4 = a3+b3=4+2=6; b4 = a3=4; t4=10\nn=5: a5 = a4+b4=6+4=10; b5 = a4=6; t5=16\nn=6: a6 = a5+b5=10+6=16; b6 = a5=10; t6=26\nn=7: a7 = a6+b6=16+10=26; b7 = a6=16; t7=42\nn=8: a8 = a7+b7=26+16=42; b8 = a7=26; t8=68\nn=9: a9 = a8+b8=42+26=68; b9 = a8=42; t9=110\nn=10: a10 = a9+b9=68+42=110; b10 = a9=68; t10=178\nn=11: a11 = a10+b10=110+68=178; b11 = a10=110; t11=288\nn=12: a12 = a11+b11=178+110=288; b12 = a11=178; t12=466\nn=13: a13 = a12+b12=288+178=466; b13 = a12=288; t13=754\n\nThus answer 754. Provide final JSON."}}],"created":1790939857,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":664,"prompt_tokens":4111,"total_tokens":4775,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-l03bSh65aFvzaoAbBlvJVHA